{
  "title": "Newton's Third Law",
  "order": 12,
  "pageType": "markdown",
  "content": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 1
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Newton's Third Law"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Introduction"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Newton's Third Law describes how forces come in pairs. Whenever one object exerts a force on another, the second object exerts an equal and opposite force back. This principle explains everything from walking to rocket propulsion."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The Law"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Newton's Third Law States:"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "blockquote",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "For every action, there is an equal and opposite reaction."
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "More precisely:"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "blockquote",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "When object A exerts a force on object B, object B exerts an equal force on object A in the opposite direction."
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Key Characteristics of Force Pairs"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The two forces in a Newton's Third Law pair:"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Are "
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "equal in magnitude",
                    "marks": [
                      {
                        "type": "bold"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Act in "
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "opposite directions",
                    "marks": [
                      {
                        "type": "bold"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Act on "
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "different objects",
                    "marks": [
                      {
                        "type": "bold"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Are of the "
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "same type",
                    "marks": [
                      {
                        "type": "bold"
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " (both gravitational, both contact, etc.)"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Act "
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "simultaneously",
                    "marks": [
                      {
                        "type": "bold"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "blockquote",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Key Concept: ",
                "marks": [
                  {
                    "type": "bold"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Newton's Third Law: For every action, there is an equal and opposite reaction. These force pairs always act on DIFFERENT objects, are the same type of force, and occur simultaneously."
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Key Concepts"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Action-Reaction Pairs"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Every force has a reaction force. These are called "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Newton's Third Law pairs",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "bold"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " or "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "action-reaction pairs",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "bold"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Examples:"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "table",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "tableRow",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "tableHeader",
                "attrs": {
                  "colspan": 1,
                  "rowspan": 1
                },
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "text",
                        "text": "Action"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "tableHeader",
                "attrs": {
                  "colspan": 1,
                  "rowspan": 1
                },
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "text",
                        "text": "Reaction"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "tableRow",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "tableCell",
                "attrs": {
                  "colspan": 1,
                  "rowspan": 1
                },
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "text",
                        "text": "Earth pulls you down (weight)"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "tableCell",
                "attrs": {
                  "colspan": 1,
                  "rowspan": 1
                },
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "text",
                        "text": "You pull Earth up"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "tableRow",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "tableCell",
                "attrs": {
                  "colspan": 1,
                  "rowspan": 1
                },
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "text",
                        "text": "Your foot pushes ground backward"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "tableCell",
                "attrs": {
                  "colspan": 1,
                  "rowspan": 1
                },
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "text",
                        "text": "Ground pushes your foot forward"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "tableRow",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "tableCell",
                "attrs": {
                  "colspan": 1,
                  "rowspan": 1
                },
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "text",
                        "text": "Rocket pushes exhaust gases down"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "tableCell",
                "attrs": {
                  "colspan": 1,
                  "rowspan": 1
                },
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "text",
                        "text": "Exhaust gases push rocket up"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "tableRow",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "tableCell",
                "attrs": {
                  "colspan": 1,
                  "rowspan": 1
                },
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "text",
                        "text": "Hammer hits nail"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "tableCell",
                "attrs": {
                  "colspan": 1,
                  "rowspan": 1
                },
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "text",
                        "text": "Nail hits hammer"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "tableRow",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "tableCell",
                "attrs": {
                  "colspan": 1,
                  "rowspan": 1
                },
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "text",
                        "text": "Magnet A attracts magnet B"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "tableCell",
                "attrs": {
                  "colspan": 1,
                  "rowspan": 1
                },
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "text",
                        "text": "Magnet B attracts magnet A"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Identifying Third Law Pairs"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "To identify a Third Law pair:"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Identify the two objects involved"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Describe the force on each object"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Check: same magnitude, opposite direction, different objects, same type"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Correct pair:",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "bold"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " \"Earth pulls apple\" and \"Apple pulls Earth\""
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "NOT a pair:",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "bold"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " \"Weight of apple\" and \"Table pushing apple up\" (different types, act on same object)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Why Don't Action-Reaction Forces Cancel?"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Forces only cancel when they act on the "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "same object",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "bold"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Third Law pairs act on "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "different objects",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "bold"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ", so they don't cancel each other."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Example: When you push a wall:"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "bulletList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "You push the wall (force on wall)"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Wall pushes you (force on you)"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "These act on different objects, so they don't cancel."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Mathematical Relationships"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Force Pair Equation"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "$$\\vec{F}_{A \\text{ on } B} = -\\vec{F}_{B \\text{ on } A}$$"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Or in terms of magnitude:"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "$$|F_{A \\text{ on } B}| = |F_{B \\text{ on } A}|$$"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Example with Numbers"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "If Earth pulls you with a force of 700 N downward:"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "bulletList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "You pull Earth with a force of 700 N upward"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "But Earth's acceleration is tiny because its mass is enormous:"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "$$a_{Earth} = \\frac{F}{m} = \\frac{700}{6 \\times 10^{24}} \\approx 10^{-22} \\text{ m/s}^2$$"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "blockquote",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Common Mistake: ",
                "marks": [
                  {
                    "type": "bold"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Weight and normal reaction are NOT a Third Law pair, even though they are equal and opposite. They act on the same object (the book). A true Third Law pair always acts on two different objects."
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Quick Check"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "quizEmbed",
        "attrs": {
          "quizId": "check-newtons-third-law"
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Worked Examples"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Example 1:",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "bold"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " Identify the Third Law pair for: \"A tennis racket exerts a 500 N force on a ball.\""
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Solution:",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "bold"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " The ball exerts a 500 N force on the tennis racket (in the opposite direction)."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Both forces:"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "bulletList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Have magnitude 500 N"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Are in opposite directions"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Are contact forces"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Act on different objects (racket and ball)"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Example 2:",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "bold"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " A 1000 kg car pushes backward on the road with a force of 4000 N. What force does the road exert on the car?"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Solution:",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "bold"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " By Newton's Third Law, the road exerts a 4000 N force forward on the car."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "This forward force accelerates the car:"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "$$a = \\frac{F}{m} = \\frac{4000}{1000} = 4 \\text{ m/s}^2$$"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Example 3:",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "bold"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " A book rests on a table. Identify all forces and their Third Law pairs."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Solution:",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "bold"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " Forces on the book:"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Weight (W):",
                    "marks": [
                      {
                        "type": "bold"
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " Earth pulls book down"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "bulletList",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "listItem",
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "paragraph",
                        "content": [
                          {
                            "type": "text",
                            "text": "Third Law pair: Book pulls Earth up"
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Normal reaction (N):",
                    "marks": [
                      {
                        "type": "bold"
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " Table pushes book up"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "bulletList",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "listItem",
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "paragraph",
                        "content": [
                          {
                            "type": "text",
                            "text": "Third Law pair: Book pushes table down"
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Note: W and N are NOT a Third Law pair (they act on the same object and are different types)."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Example 4:",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "bold"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " A 70 kg astronaut in space pushes against a 10 kg toolbox with a force of 20 N. Find the acceleration of each."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Solution:",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "bold"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " Forces: Astronaut pushes toolbox (20 N), toolbox pushes astronaut (20 N opposite)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Toolbox acceleration:"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "blockquote",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Remember: ",
                "marks": [
                  {
                    "type": "bold"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "To identify a Third Law pair, check three things: (1) the forces act on different objects, (2) they are the same type of force, and (3) they are equal in size but opposite in direction."
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Quick Check"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "quizEmbed",
        "attrs": {
          "quizId": "check-newtons-third-law-2"
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "$$a = \\frac{20}{10} = 2 \\text{ m/s}^2$$ (away from astronaut)\n\nAstronaut acceleration:\n$$a = \\frac{20}{70} = 0.29 \\text{ m/s}^2$$ (away from toolbox)\n\nBoth move apart, but the toolbox accelerates faster.\n\n## Applications\n\n### Walking\n\n1. Your foot pushes backward on the ground\n2. The ground pushes forward on your foot (Third Law)\n3. This forward force accelerates you\n\n```\n       Person\n        /|\\\n       / | \\\n      /  |  \\\n     /   |   \\\n    /    |    \\\n   ------+------\n   Foot pushes     Ground pushes\n   ground BACKWARD foot FORWARD\n   <--- F1         F2 --->\n\n   F1 = F2 (Third Law pair)\n   The forward force F2 accelerates the person\n```\n\n### Swimming\n\n1. Hands push water backward\n2. Water pushes hands (and swimmer) forward\n\n### Rocket Propulsion\n\n1. Rocket pushes exhaust gases downward\n2. Exhaust gases push rocket upward\n\nThis works even in the vacuum of space because the reaction force acts on the rocket, not on air.\n\n### Recoil\n\nWhen a gun fires:\n1. Gun pushes bullet forward\n2. Bullet pushes gun backward (recoil)\n\nBoth forces have equal magnitude, but the gun has much more mass, so it accelerates less.\n\n## Common Misconceptions\n\n1. **\"Action and reaction cancel out\"** — They act on DIFFERENT objects, so they cannot cancel.\n\n2. **\"The reaction happens after the action\"** — Both forces occur simultaneously. \"Action\" and \"reaction\" are just names; neither comes first.\n\n3. **\"Weight and normal reaction are a Third Law pair\"** — No! They act on the same object. Weight pairs with the object pulling Earth; normal reaction pairs with the object pushing the surface.\n\n4. **\"Heavier objects exert more force\"** — The forces are always equal. The heavier object accelerates less because of its greater mass.\n\n5. **\"Rockets push against the air\"** — Rockets work by pushing exhaust gases. They work in space where there's no air.\n\n6. **\"If forces are equal, nothing moves\"** — Objects move based on the NET force ON THEM. Third Law pairs act on different objects.\n\n## Summary\n\n- Newton's Third Law: Every action has an equal and opposite reaction\n- Third Law pairs are equal in magnitude, opposite in direction, same type, act on different objects\n- Forces don't cancel because they act on different objects\n- Applications: walking, swimming, rockets, recoil\n- Weight and normal reaction are NOT a Third Law pair\n- Both forces in a pair act simultaneously\n- Equal forces on different masses cause different accelerations\n\n"
          }
        ]
